  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABG-Realising the Faith Potential</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be carried out in  four Arch Dioceses in Kenya,covering a total of 25 Catholic dioceses at different levels ie Eldoret, Embu, Garissa, Homa Bay, Isiolo, Kakamega, Kericho, Kisii, Kisumu, Kitale, Kitui, Lodwar, Machakos, Malindi, Maralal, Marsabit, Meru, Mombasa, Muranga, Nairobi, Nakuru, Ngong, Nyeri and Nyaururu.The project however shall concentrate on the diocese of Marsabit,Isiolo and Maralal.
The legal holder will be Kenya Episcopal Conference Catholic Secretariat.  The project will be under Governance and Democracy Programme within Catholic Justice and Peace Commission. 
The project will seek to improve governance in Kenya in four dioceses by carrying out intensive civil campaigns, development of a simplified version for Constitutional Education during diocesan Workshops and disseminating this information throughout the established church structures.
The project also sees a strong connection between governance and justice and will therefore carry out advocacy before the TJRC Bill becomes an Act as the current draft is seriously flawed, ensuring the participation and inputs of all Kenyans to the bill.
The project will be involved in the lobbying and support of activities that shall improve governance. This shall include, lobbying for a responsive legal structures, supporting the victims, survivors and perpetrators of conflicts, providing the legal advice and psycho-social support. 
 As an advocacy unit the project recognises the importance of research and shall carry out research, including conflict mapping and document the process to produce a comprehensive report that can inform others in future.
To attain high quality work the project shall train its National office in Project Proposal writing, Monitoring an Evaluation, Statistical Package for Social Sciences and training in conformity to International Reporting Standards</narrative>
  </description>
